    "q-137038": {
      "dom_id": "step-q137038",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "What is the missing number in the following equality?\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\times 2\\,\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{\\,\\boxed{}}{15}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write $2\\,\\frac{3}{5}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{(2\\times 5)+3}{5}=\\frac{13}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\times \\frac{13}{5}=\\frac{1\\times 13}{3\\times 5}=\\frac{13}{15}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing number is $13.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
