    "q-198150": {
      "dom_id": "step-q198150",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Expressed as a fraction in lowest terms, $\\frac{2}{7}\\times 3\\,\\frac{1}{3}=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write $3\\,\\frac{1}{3}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n3\\,\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{(3\\times 3)+1}{3}=\\frac{10}{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{7}\\times \\frac{10}{3}=\\frac{2\\times 10}{7\\times 3}=\\frac{20}{21}\n$$",
