    "q-137045": {
      "dom_id": "step-q137045",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$\\frac{5}{8}\\times 1\\,\\frac{1}{2}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{1}{2}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{(1\\times 2)+1}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{8}\\times \\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{5\\times 3}{8\\times 2}=\\frac{15}{16}\n$$",
