    "q-57114": {
      "dom_id": "step-q57114",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Determine the missing number in the following equality.\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{5}\\times \\frac{6}{7}=1\\,\\frac{\\,\\boxed{}}{35}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{1}{5}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{(1\\times 5)+1}{5}=\\frac{6}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{5}\\times \\frac{6}{7}=\\frac{6\\times 6}{5\\times 7}=\\frac{36}{35}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{36}{35}=1\\,\\text{R}1=1\\,\\frac{1}{35}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing number is $1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
