    "q-137103": {
      "dom_id": "step-q137103",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "$\\frac{4}{5}\\times 2\\,\\frac{1}{7}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write $2\\,\\frac{1}{7}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{1}{7}=\\frac{(2\\times 7)+1}{7}=\\frac{15}{7}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5}\\times \\frac{15}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this product by swapping the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5}\\times \\frac{15}{7} & =\\frac{4}{7}\\times \\frac{15}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{7}\\times \\text{ }3 \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12}{7}=1\\,\\text{R}5=1\\,\\frac{5}{7}\n$$",
